# fixtures/lq/cases/design-blocks.cases: the 44 LQ code blocks of [50] (WP-22, R-FIX): the example of [50 §0.2],
# the 35 query and TX blocks of [50 §2.9] (Q1-Q29; Q17 is a JSON string, not a code block) and the 8 DEFINE
# statements of [50 §4.1] (7) and [50 §4.3] (1), each parsed on its own as [50 §11] (assemble2.py) did.
# Every block parses with its entry symbol; the token stream is asserted ([LQ/lexical §11]). Where [LQ/json-ir §7]
# gives the tree of a block, the S-AST and the JSON IR output form are asserted too.
# The blocks are the design's text: the [LQ/std] versions of the DEFINEs differ ([LQ/std §4]) and are in std.cases.
# Format: fixtures/lq/INDEX.md §2.

